' --- log: the Boost.Log front end

class ores::telemetry::log::telemetry_sink_backend {
    +telemetry_sink_backend(res : shared_ptr<domain::resource>, handler : log_record_handler)
    +consume(rec : record_view) : void
}
note right of "ores::telemetry::log::telemetry_sink_backend"
The sink backend the automated pass dropped: its base clause
wraps onto a second line, which the parser does not follow. It
converts each Boost.Log record into a domain::log_record, reads
the trace_id and span_id attributes for correlation, and skips a
record marked SkipTelemetry.
end note

class ores::telemetry::log::database_sink_backend {
    +database_sink_backend(resource : shared_ptr<domain::resource>, handler : database_log_handler, source_type : string, source_name : string)
    +consume(rec : record_view) : void
    +set_session_id(session_id : uuid) : void
    +set_account_id(account_id : uuid) : void
}
note right of "ores::telemetry::log::database_sink_backend"
The second backend the parser dropped. It converts each record
into messaging::telemetry_log_entry and hands it to the handler,
which the database part supplies. The two setters stamp a
session or account id onto the entries it produces.
end note

